# SetVuiBrightness
#
# Forwarder service around Unitree Go2 VUI SetBrightness
# (api_id=1005) over `unitree::robot::go2::VuiClient::SetBrightness(level)`,
# range 0-10 (VUI 屏幕亮度,0=dimmest, 10=brightest).
#
# Why a separate bridge node:
# `lgw_bt_planner`'s SetLedBrightnessNode used to call the SDK directly
# in-process; on the dev container that caused bt_runner to SIGSEGV
# (exit code -11) when BT instantiated the node — the in-process SDK
# DomainParticipant collided with the rclcpp rmw_cyclonedds_cpp
# DomainParticipant (cyclone DDS 0.10.x in-process double-participant
# issue). Isolating the SDK into a dedicated rclcpp node keeps the SDK
# DDS DomainParticipant in its own process; the BT side then becomes
# a thin BT::RosServiceNode<SetVuiBrightness> (which is exactly the
# pattern already used for SetBodyPose → body_pose_bridge).
#
# Schema is intentionally small (one int + ack) because the underlying
# SDK call has no rich payload — it's a fire-and-forget state setter
# (1s synchronous RPC timeout, ret==0 means the firmware acked).
#
# Caller's BT node on FAILURE branch lets the operator see the
# firmware-inaccessible state without crashing bt_runner.
int32 level
---
bool success
string message
